Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 6.1: an inheritance clause that does not appear within
   an enclosing class "is evaluated as if it was a top level expression.
   Consequently, it will almost certainly fail since no interesting classes
   are available at top level" -- a top level expression (3.8) has no
   enclosing object to send to. So a module's root class may inherit only
   Object or Value, or write Object <: Value; every other root clause is a
   defect (`docs/design/object-model.md`, "The root rule").

   The refusal is deferred to instantiation: the module loads, its class
   exists and can be inspected, and only an instance is refused -- which
   `run` asks for first, so `main:args:` never runs. *)
class RootNamesAnUnknownClass usingPlatform: platformAtCreation = Missing new () (
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: 'unreachable'; newLine
    )
) : ()
